WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.080
Speaker 1: I do need to start today with an
apology for everything I've ever said on the

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.109
show that has upset somebody.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:09.390
No, I'm kidding.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.100
I want to apologize because I did a little
bit of a cleaning in the studio.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.900
You could call it sort of a bleaching of sorts.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:25.199
And I didn't realize that two furniture elements
that are normally separated where my microphone

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:29.830
is connected to something that is nowhere
near me just so I can't inadvertently create

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.930
any gunk in the audio to think two elements
were touching that should not have been touching

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.040
the last two days.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:42.390
And I didn't even realize that I was regularly
creating a sort of above noise with the microphone.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:48.180
People sent me, as you can imagine, extremely
polite messages about it and I've resolved

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.640
it, OK, I've resolved it.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.400
So I do want to apologize for that.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.170
But let's not dwell on the negative.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:01:00.750
We are really starting to get to the next
phase, which I would believe to be the end

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:07.500
phase of the coronavirus pandemic as cases
are now down nearly 90 percent in the United

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.650
States, deaths are down nearly 85 percent.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:18.470
But but but vaccination continues to slow
down, as there are now way more vaccines in

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.770
the US than the number of people that seem
to want them, at least relatively quickly,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:23.830
which is sad.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.360
And we're going to talk about that.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.210
Much of that lack of demand is because of
Republicans.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.470
This isn't a bipartisan thing.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.700
Four percent of Democrats don't want the vaccine.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.710
Forty one percent of Republicans don't want
the vaccine, as we discussed yesterday.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.830
Let's go through the case and death numbers
as we now have them.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:47.330
Cases in the United States peaking in mid-January,
around two hundred and fifty five thousand

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.540
a day now down to an average of 32000 a day.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.180
That is a decline of about 87 percent from
that pandemic peak.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:04.120
There are some states where cases are there,
not literally zero, but they are almost statistically

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.860
zero places like California that now have
really, really low rates.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:13.160
And they're continuing down as more and more
people get vaccinated.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:22.160
In terms of deaths, things are not yet looking
as good deaths lag changes in cases by about

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.790
three to four weeks.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:29.540
But nevertheless, deaths are now down about
82 percent from a pandemic peak in late January.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.330
We were at thirty four fifty a day.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:38.200
That's like 9/11, plus 10 percent every day
in deaths in late January.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.240
We are now down to just a hair over 600 deaths
a day.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.090
Still way too high to be calling this anything
close to over.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.170
But the right direction continues and that
direction is down.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.120
Now, one factor that is slowing down the decline
is that fewer and fewer people are getting

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.560
vaccinated each day.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.940
This is not because there aren't enough vaccines
or not enough appointments.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.770
Just about every state, many pharmacy chains,
chains, many locations have switched to just

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:05.890
show up.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.060
No appointment needed.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.750
Just get over here and we'll give you a vaccine.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.310
We have more than enough vaccines to go around.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:17.060
We have vaccines here like countries around
the world are dreaming of having.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.300
That's not an exaggeration.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:25.550
But forty one percent of Republicans and twenty
four percent of all Americans don't want the

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.550
vaccine.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:33.090
And so after peaking at about three point
three million doses per day in early April,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:38.410
we have seen almost a 50 percent decline to
now just one point eight million doses per

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.680
day.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.390
This is embarrassing.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.190
Look around the world.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:47.410
Countries around the world are doing everything
they can to get vaccines.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.220
There are countries that are happy to get
half a million vaccines.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:55.400
We have millions and millions of them just
sitting around ready.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.670
And we have millions and millions of people
saying, no, I don't want to get one.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:05.180
The cases and the deaths would decline way
more quickly if more people got vaccinated.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.530
Just think we're vaccinating about half of
the number we were vaccinating a month ago.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:14.060
Each day we could be seeing cases decline
significantly faster.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.989
If we just got back to where we were three
point three million vaccines per day, we could

00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:21.579
open everything sooner and more safely if
more people got vaccinated.

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:23.969
Now, what's going on globally?

00:04:23.969 --> 00:04:29.680
Because the US led from the standpoint of
bad early in the pandemic, we are now leading

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.800
from the standpoint of good in terms of the
vaccination.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.620
But the U.S. is not the world.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.639
What's going on with global numbers?

00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:42.490
The good news is that global cases and global
deaths are now clearly starting to come down.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.860
Ten days ago, it looked like they were leveling
off.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.419
But where will things go?

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:51.129
Globally, cases peaked at about eight hundred
and thirty thousand cases per day in later

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:52.139
April.

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:55.229
We're now down to about six hundred and sixty
five thousand a day.

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:57.849
It's an outrageous number, but it's down.

00:04:57.849 --> 00:05:04.169
20 percent from the peak, that's good global
deaths similarly to the picture in the US,

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:08.189
global deaths are declining, but lagging the
case decline.

00:05:08.189 --> 00:05:11.550
Global deaths peaked at about 14000 a day
back in January.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.820
Can you imagine?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:18.479
Almost got back there in April and we are
now down to about 12000 deaths a day.

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:21.479
That's a decline of 15 percent from the peak.

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:24.150
But there is a long way to go globally.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:30.550
And part of why it's so depressing to know
that we have the vaccines for everyone.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:37.360
But to see in the United States people opting
out is that the vaccines are why the US is

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.509
doing better and better.

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:43.869
This is a very similar thing to the measles
anti vaccine, and it's depressing.

00:05:43.869 --> 00:05:45.550
Doesn't even really cut it.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:50.309
You have measles and TIV actors who say who
dies of measles?

00:05:50.309 --> 00:05:53.009
Why would I go and get my kid vaccinated for
measles?

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:58.659
The reason almost no one dies of measles is
the vaccination campaign has been so effective

00:05:58.659 --> 00:06:01.360
and the vaccine is so effective.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.009
Were it not for that, then people would be
dying of measles.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:08.909
People are saying some cases are going down,
this is ending.

00:06:08.909 --> 00:06:10.729
I don't need to get the vaccine.

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:14.599
But the reason why they're going down is we
have so many vaccines.

00:06:14.599 --> 00:06:17.899
It's a privilege to have access to so many
vaccines.

00:06:17.899 --> 00:06:19.750
An incredible headline.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:25.430
Multiple states reported zero covid deaths
on single days over the last week for the

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:26.809
first time in months.

00:06:26.809 --> 00:06:30.749
This includes Arizona, Minnesota, Massachusetts,
Maryland and others.

00:06:30.749 --> 00:06:36.400
Now, of course, weekend reporting can throw
off the meaning of any single day's data,

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.789
but the averages are declining, things are
opening.

00:06:39.789 --> 00:06:41.520
And that is all great.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.939
Just go and get vaccinated.

00:06:42.939 --> 00:06:43.939
It's free.

00:06:43.939 --> 00:06:44.939
You just show up.

00:06:44.939 --> 00:06:49.589
There's a vaccine available and maybe this
will be more of an incentive for people to

00:06:49.589 --> 00:06:55.569
get vaccinated, although I think the people
not getting vaccinated don't care about this.

00:06:55.569 --> 00:07:01.619
The European Union has announced hours ago
they will be opening to vaccinated Americans.

00:07:01.619 --> 00:07:02.690
Let's talk about that next

